  "details": "\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: Heap-based buffer overflow in function utf_ptr2char\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2022-2182.patch:  When on line zero check\n     the column is valid for line one in do_one_cmd function\n     - CVE-2022-2182\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: Out-of-bounds read in function get_lisp_indent\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2022-2183.patch: Add check to avoid going over\n     the NUL at the end of the line in get_lisp_indent function\n     - CVE-2022-2183\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: Heap-based buffer overflow in function ins_bs\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2022-2207.patch: Check the cursor column\n     is more than zero in ins_bs function\n     - CVE-2022-2207\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: Out-of-bound write in function ml_append_int\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2022-2210.patch: Use zero offset when change\n     removes all lines in a diff block in diff_mark_adjust_tp function\n     - CVE-2022-2210",
